---
description: Use project skills for feature-module work.
alwaysApply: true
---

When creating or expanding an Angular 21+ feature module, read and follow `.agents/skills/angular-module-scaffold/SKILL.md`. The OpenAPI contract must already be approved. Keep a `doc.md` in the root of each feature module and consult `.spec/memory/` before implementation.

When starting the Angular frontend, read and follow `.agents/skills/angular-frontend-scaffold/SKILL.md`. Ask for the project name when absent, use its deterministic generator, and validate only by build; do not run tests, a development server, or an API.

When implementing or reviewing Angular UI, read and follow `.agents/skills/angular-tailwind-ui-specialist/SKILL.md`. Use Tailwind CSS, semantic HTML, mobile-first responsive behavior, accessible controls, and the Neon Graphite design tokens. Keep business rules and HTTP out of templates.

For Java persistence work involving JPA/Hibernate, SQL performance, transactions, concurrency, PostgreSQL, or Flyway, read `.agents/skills/java-persistence-performance/SKILL.md` and only its relevant references. Preserve approved specs, Clean Architecture, `owner_id` isolation, and PostgreSQL/Testcontainers conventions.

